        a.accept("info.bettacraft.lithops", "Two fat leaves that look like a pebble, with a yellow flower from the cleft. Grows very slowly and rots in humid air.\nDry and hot: 10-45 % humidity, 20-38 °C, strong light. Plant it on soil, sand or gravel on the land of a terrarium or paludarium: it grows there by the light, the humidity and the air temperature, spreads (offsets around it) and keeps the air humid; in a bad climate it languishes. Outside a tank it is a decoration that does not grow.\nFind it: in deserts and badlands; rarely from the wandering trader.\nShears: take an offset (a small rooted plant).");
